<title>USA: Krantor plans 1-for-25 reverse split.</title>
<headline>Krantor plans 1-for-25 reverse split.</headline>
<dateline>DEER PARK, N.Y. 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Krantor Corp said on Friday that it plans to effect a one for 25 reverse stock split, since its low price may jeopardize its listing.</p>
<p>The company's shareholders will vote on the plan at the company's annual meeting, scheduled on April 30, 1997, Krantor said.</p>
<p>The company would have 1,054,133 shares outstanding after the reverse split, down from 26,363,333, Krantor said.</p>
<p>Management believes that the company's low share price would jeopardize its listing on the Nasdaq Small Cap market unless the stock price increases to $1 or more, Krantor said.</p>
